{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1512776-can-a-vampire-build-himself-a-living-body-with-vicissitude-6","id":1512776,"title":"Can a vampire build himself a living body with Vicissitude 6?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-25T14:55:04-07:00","id":1512776,"title":"Can a vampire build himself a living body with Vicissitude 6?","content":"From Player's Guide to the High Clans:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With normal Vicissitude, a Tzimisce may take the arm from one person and graft it to another, but the recipient is unable to control the arm and it soon begins to decay. With this power, the user may take body parts from living creatures and graft them on to others, living or undead, and allow for the recipient to use the new limb. Exceptionally monstrous and disturbing creatures can be created with this power or one may graft extra organs into others, allowing them to function longer while wounded.<br /> <br /> <b>System:</b> Removing a limb requires an Intelligence + Body Crafts roll (difficulty 6). Extracting an organ is an extended Intelligence + Body Crafts roll (difficulty 7), with 10 successes required and each roll representing an hour of work. The process of grafting must then begin within an hour. or the limb or organ dies. Attachment is an extended roll of Intelligence + Body Crafts (difficulty 7), requiring 10 successes and each roll representing half an hour's work. Attaching an appropriate limb, such as a human arm to a human, is difficulty 7. Attaching an inappropriate limb, such as horse legs to a human, is difficulty 8. Inserting organs is difficulty 9. Attaching limbs to a vampire is somewhat easier (difficulty 6). Theoretically, one could put organs inside a vampire, but this has no effect.<br /> <br /> The effect of attaching extra limbs is entirely up to the Storyteller. Extra arms might help in grappling and multiple attacks and extra legs might aid stability but the main effect is generally freakishness rather than effectiveness, since coordinating the extra limbs is very difficult. Extra organs grant the recipient an additional wounded health level per organ, though a maximum of two can be grafted.<br /> \u200b </div> </div> </div><br /> So, could a vampire replace his undead body piece by piece with limbs, muscles, bones, organs ecc. untill he has an almost-completely alive body and achieve something similar to life?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T15:20:55-07:00","id":1512778,"title":"","content":"Since it mentions that organs fail when implanted into the undead, I think the answer is &quot;no&quot;. My reading is that while you can, for example, add another pair of arms and those arms become part of you, that they are as undead as your original pair are. Besides, if you want to mimic life, the blush of life and the domino of life ritual are both much easier.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">Though on similar lines, I have wondered that if you used vicissitude to merge yourself with a ghoul, and that ghoul was still alive but helpless to do anything as you piloted your shared body around, could you kind of seem alive? For example, if you attach your oesophagus to their stomach and swallow food, then their stomach could digest it, right? You could use auspex to share their senses, replace your tongue with theirs to taste food, use their reproductive system to have kids...<br /> And if you wear a ghoul as a meat suit, does this protect you from sunlight?</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-25T15:49:30-07:00","id":1512785,"title":"","content":"A thing to consider is that vampirism is a curse on the soul itself, replacing the body parts won't give you a complete work around.<br /> <br /> A good example of this is a vampire using Thaumaturgy Path of Summoning to create a living body duplicate of themselves and then use Dominate to put their mind/soul into the body. Sure, you are not going to burn in sunlight, but you are still going to rolling for freak outs and staying awake the whole time.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, an ST might consider the concept that if you over mod your body to the point that it is considered normal/mortal, there is the a chance that your vampiric soul might disconnect. The result being like if your body was destroyed while you were possessing a mortal or you were astral projecting with Auspex. You can't regain willpower and slowly decay until you meet final death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T00:07:07-07:00","id":1512831,"title":"","content":"Parallel to this, something that came to my mind is that if it is possible to create these bodies with vicissitude, would it be possible to create a functional body but without a soul? in this case, could ghosts possess the body? Demons could occupy them even if they had no memories it would still be a functional body for them I guess. That could breed a strange kind of cooperation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T02:15:03-07:00","id":1512842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1512776-can-a-vampire-build-himself-a-living-body-with-vicissitude-6#post1512776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, could a vampire replace his undead body piece by piece with limbs, muscles, bones, organs ecc. untill he has an almost-completely alive body and achieve something similar to life?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really<br /> If you remove the arm of a living person and graft it to another living one, thats &quot;simple&quot;, you graft it to a living body, the work represents the rewiring of nerves and blood vessels<br /> Life ot Life<br /> But if you graft it to an undead/dead? That body part, without oxygen, nutrition,blood circulation... the bodypart or organ simply dies eventually in my opinion (and even a vampire is able to make its heart pump, the organs are - especially in the DA setting where this is from - useless and withered if not outright vomited out - a vampire simply lack the &quot;inner apparatus&quot; to keep alive a living part)<br /> Or/and Cainite vitae transfoms it, making the part of you, either &quot;ghouling&quot; that part, sustaining with the power of the vitae or simply make the part of your undead body<br /> Normally a vampire's body &quot;restes itself&quot; every morning, tattoos dissapear, piercings; the body is back to the state it was when it was Embaced - Vicissitude overwrite this<br /> But on realistic levels? You can't cheat the Curse, even on the Path of Metamorphosis and Vicissitude...<br /> ...<br /> ..<br /> .<br /> Now the Eldest, true, basically became a living organism, first became the god-tree, during the Dark Ages, something quasi-living thing annd then under New York, it entered a meditative state to reach Metamorphosis. In the process, its body dissolved to a puddle of slime, then transformed into fungi, then into plants and every other living creature in existence, exploring the infinitude of life by assuming its shape. The Eldest fed on its own creations, Zantosa Revenants, and clueless Nosferatu, as it expanded in size and complexity. It produced its own vitae, finding sustenance in the very essence of the Earth, slowly approaching the final transformation, ultimately bacme &quot;alive&quot;. Finally in Gehenna, it was described, its consciousness left the body, witch eventually regressed back to an unliving state. <br /> A bit similar happened with the Eldes's child, Demdemeh, who transformed himself into a viral form, partitioning himself into various strings and infecting other viruses like Ebola in order to spread his essence. It is said that much of the African wildlife is infected with him and a group of researchers of the University of Marburg brought the virus 1967 into Europe, although greater consequences have not yet been seen. It is said that various &quot;elephants' graveyards&quot; are actually parts of Demdemeh that strive to reunite with the whole. - arguably, the Demdemeh\u200b &quot;virus&quot; is not undead at this point - or if it is, then god, that is terrifying","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T03:07:12-07:00","id":1512849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1512776-can-a-vampire-build-himself-a-living-body-with-vicissitude-6?p=1512831#post1512831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Parallel to this, something that came to my mind is that if it is possible to create these bodies with vicissitude, would it be possible to create a functional body but without a soul? in this case, could ghosts possess the body? Demons could occupy them even if they had no memories it would still be a functional body for them I guess. That could breed a strange kind of cooperation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't think of a given example of this, but it should be possible. We know that some Spirits/Demons/Ghosts have no problem possessing corpses, so they don't even require a fully functional body. Depending on type of the ephemeral creature, the possession may be more like puppeteering a container rather than 'becoming', though. The same type may just as well go for any fresh corpse or construct rather than a bespoke body, but I can see the appeal. If we're going into soul transfer territory though, P:tC is entirely built around that premise. From what I have read of it, it's a pretty neat game; though I don't know how well a crossover with oWoD would work.<br /> <br /> I've been looking into constructs (ie, magically animated bodies or statues) lately and it's a surprisingly broad topic if you include necromantic applications. I would certainly think creating something like a flesh golem with Vicissitude should be possible.<br /> <br /> Aside on constructs: there's a few lines in the myth of <a href=\"https://etcsl.orinst.ox.ac.uk/section1/tr141.htm\" target=\"_blank\">Inanna's descent into the underworld</a> where Enki creates two possible constructs from the &quot;dirt under his fingernails&quot; for a task in the underworld (because they are neither dead nor alive, they can enter and leave freely). Thinking about what two multi-millennia old constructs are up to these days is a pretty fun story seed, I thought- especially if you swap in the usual noddist vampire substitutes (Enki=Enoch, Inanna=Ishtar=Arikel etc)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T04:02:41-07:00","id":1512852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With normal Vicissitude, a Tzimisce may take the arm from one person and graft it to another, but the recipient is unable to control the arm and it soon begins to decay. With this power, the user may take body parts from living creatures and graft them on to others, living or undead, and allow for the recipient to use the new limb. </div> </div> </div>The whole point of the power is being able to graft parts who still live and are functional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T06:03:56-07:00","id":1512858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1512776-can-a-vampire-build-himself-a-living-body-with-vicissitude-6?p=1512831#post1512831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Parallel to this, something that came to my mind is that if it is possible to create these bodies with vicissitude, would it be possible to create a functional body but without a soul? in this case, could ghosts possess the body? Demons could occupy them even if they had no memories it would still be a functional body for them I guess. That could breed a strange kind of cooperation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes actually. There's a flaw specifically for this called &quot;Soulless&quot;.<br /> <br /> Depending on edition there's some flavor text of not having emotions, but the main issue with not having a soul is not being able to use magic(to the point you don't even count as a sleeper against mages because your will doesn't have any effect on consensus). This would likely have horrible effects on the embrace considering vampires are dead/time-adjacent bodies animated by by the fact their souls are kind of trapped in their blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T07:37:47-07:00","id":1512866,"title":"","content":"Unrelated question... in the OWod, can a ghost manage to possess permanently a suitable vessel ( a soulless body ) and... well, return to life?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T07:50:45-07:00","id":1512869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1512776-can-a-vampire-build-himself-a-living-body-with-vicissitude-6?p=1512866#post1512866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unrelated question... in the OWod, can a ghost manage to possess permanently a suitable vessel ( a soulless body ) and... well, return to life?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and No.<br /> <br /> Technically yes because there's definitely ways to do it if you dig deep enough into the more obscure rituals and start combining them(or just hire a mage), and here's also a special spectre arcanoi specifically for this, but also mostly no because that's not something a ghost capable of by itself and the previously mentioned arcanoi wasn't talked about in W20(which completely re-did the arcanoi to the irritation of many fans).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T08:26:06-07:00","id":1512876,"title":"","content":"Puppetry 5 allows a Wraith to literally kill the soul of a host and take over the body. Arguably an already soulless body would grant the same benefits without the struggle, as there is nothing to resist the takeover. It's hinted though that coming truly back to live is insanely difficult or impossible- a body taken over with the aforementioned method is starting to decay, as the oblivion taint of the Shadow permeates it. The Risen Eurydice tried and got seven heartbeats for her efforts, which included a ritual with blood of a 4th gen vampire.<br /> <br /> If you count Hsien as 'ghosts', inhabiting a soulless body (or rather, slipping in while the original is on their way out) is par of the course for them. I would probably classify them closer to spirits, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T10:21:48-07:00","id":1512889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Conradine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1512776-can-a-vampire-build-himself-a-living-body-with-vicissitude-6?p=1512852#post1512852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The whole point of the power is being able to graft parts who still live and are functional.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you can graft a living body part from one living being onto another living being, and that new body part will function and be alive.<br /> <br /> You can graft a living body part from one living being onto another undead being, and that body part will function, but the text you quoted says nothing about it *remaining* alive.<br /> <br /> I'm also assuming that you can graft an undead body part from one undead being to another, and the new body part would function (I just need to double-check the rules on how long detached Kindred body parts remain whole, assuming Vicissitude does not &quot;cover&quot; that).<br /> <br /> The interesting question would be grafting an undead body part onto a living being. Would it be functional but remain undead? Would it come back to life? Would it become a necrotic monstrosity that needs to be surgically removed in order to save the recipient?<br /> <br /> These are the rocks upon which we build the church of Metamorphosis <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T11:34:24-07:00","id":1512895,"title":"","content":"My idea with the power was for players with characters of the right generation to do the kind of weird-ass, multi-limbed creatures that got tjrown around a lot in art and fiction text regarding the Tzimisce.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance Writer and Storyteller's Vault contributor. Find my work here: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/index.php?affiliate_id=17903\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.storytellersvault.com/ind...liate_id=17903</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1535-jackob","name":"Jackob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1535_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T12:22:44-07:00","id":1512901,"title":"","content":"<i> Theoretically, one could put organs inside a vampire, but this has no effect.</i><br /> <br /> I think this is in the context of mechanical effects, since giving extra organs to living things does have mechanical effects, but perhaps giving a vampire a heart would give them a pulse, or giving them a complete digestive system would allow them to eat. With the later, you could already use vicissitude to give yourself a nice storage cavity, so it's not a massive stretch. <br /> <br /> Crazy ideas:<br /> Perhaps if you could give yourself a closed-human blood system where the blood never goes stale you could use that to your benefit for rituals. <br /> <br /> <br /> Vozhd yourself, use other parts of the Vozhd to keep rituals like Domino of life or virgin-blood-facemask always on, or your subordinate lives can do the grisly ritual stuff like eating flesh that you'd normally have to vomit out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T15:17:41-07:00","id":1512914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1512776-can-a-vampire-build-himself-a-living-body-with-vicissitude-6?p=1512901#post1512901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i> Theoretically, one could put organs inside a vampire, but this has no effect.</i><br /> <br /> I think this is in the context of mechanical effects, since giving extra organs to living things does have mechanical effects, but perhaps giving a vampire a heart would give them a pulse, or giving them a complete digestive system would allow them to eat. With the later, you could already use vicissitude to give yourself a nice storage cavity, so it's not a massive stretch.<br /> <br /> Crazy ideas:<br /> Perhaps if you could give yourself a closed-human blood system where the blood never goes stale you could use that to your benefit for rituals.<br /> <br /> <br /> Vozhd yourself, use other parts of the Vozhd to keep rituals like Domino of life or virgin-blood-facemask always on, or your subordinate lives can do the grisly ritual stuff like eating flesh that you'd normally have to vomit out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've thought about something similar, like adding more muscle tissue to increase physical strength and endurance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T16:28:36-07:00","id":1512924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1512776-can-a-vampire-build-himself-a-living-body-with-vicissitude-6?p=1512901#post1512901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[I]<br /> Crazy ideas:<br /> Perhaps if you could give yourself a closed-human blood system where the blood never goes stale you could use that to your benefit for rituals.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's actually a canon item that does just that and it's featured in a minor role in Bloodlines to give the player a mild blood regen(forgot the name though).<br /> <br /> Granted, the fact Tsimisce can strap creatures miniaturized with Vis to themselves and gain effectively unlimited BP is one of those setting elements you have to hand-wave to not break the setting itself(of which there are unfortunately Many examples in classic WOD across all splats).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-26T19:40:28-07:00","id":1512928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1512776-can-a-vampire-build-himself-a-living-body-with-vicissitude-6?p=1512849#post1512849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can't think of a given example of this, but it should be possible. We know that some Spirits/Demons/Ghosts have no problem possessing corpses, so they don't even require a fully functional body. Depending on type of the ephemeral creature, the possession may be more like puppeteering a container rather than 'becoming', though. The same type may just as well go for any fresh corpse or construct rather than a bespoke body, but I can see the appeal. If we're going into soul transfer territory though, P:tC is entirely built around that premise. From what I have read of it, it's a pretty neat game; though I don't know how well a crossover with oWoD would work.<br /> <br /> I've been looking into constructs (ie, magically animated bodies or statues) lately and it's a surprisingly broad topic if you include necromantic applications. I would certainly think creating something like a flesh golem with Vicissitude should be possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now it occurred to me what if a Tzimisce created a blood bond with a sorcerer who knew the name of a fallen one and used that relationship to control him indirectly, it's even possible to repeat this process a few times.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T04:43:44-07:00","id":1512942,"title":"","content":"Threads like these remind me why I removed Vicissitude from my games","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T06:31:05-07:00","id":1512948,"title":"","content":"My opinion...<br /> <br /> Vicissitude 6 is the kind of power only an elder can achieve. I find acceptable that it allows to graft living parts to an undead vampire.<br /> There's to say that vampire - with few exceptions like Samedi or specific flaws - are <b>not </b>rotting corpse. They're &quot;trapped in stasis&quot;, but they don't rot and the simple fact that a vampire metabolic functions can be briefly reactivated strongly suggest the vampiric body is not dead tissue.<br /> According to Beckett's Diary there is even some minimal cellular replication, and with thin bloods being able to occasionally reproduce I think that vampires can be firmly placed on a whole different category from Risen and zombies.<br /> <br /> Living parts grafted to a vampire body would almost certainly be &quot;ghouled&quot;, sustained and even regenerated by the power of Vitae. But ghouls are still fundamentally living, so those parts would still be supernaturally living tissue.<br /> <br /> <br /> - - -<br /> <br /> I would love to know more about the opposite experiment, the Wolves in Sheep's clothing route from Winter's Teeth. What would happen to a ghoul who replace most of his body with vampiric parts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T06:42:28-07:00","id":1512949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1512776-can-a-vampire-build-himself-a-living-body-with-vicissitude-6?p=1512942#post1512942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Threads like these remind me why I removed Vicissitude from my games</div> </div> </div> </div>It's so bad?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T09:14:21-07:00","id":1512967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1512776-can-a-vampire-build-himself-a-living-body-with-vicissitude-6?p=1512942#post1512942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Threads like these remind me why I removed Vicissitude from my games</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In the deffense of Vicissitude (and any other Discipline) it is not the power itself that is &quot;bad&quot; or &quot;unbalanced&quot;, but 99% of te time it is the players who tend to forget, Vampire is a personal horror game and the Disciplines <i>are part of the Curse , </i>steering you away from who you were, from Humanity, slowly degenerating you in to something not even remotely human and not &quot;superpowers&quot; ready to abuse","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T11:57:34-07:00","id":1512990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1512776-can-a-vampire-build-himself-a-living-body-with-vicissitude-6?p=1512942#post1512942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Threads like these remind me why I removed Vicissitude from my games</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm the opposite. Graft life-to-life is such a cool power that I make it an alternative level 5 power. That said, I do run wild with the idea that Vicissitude is a forbidden power that the establishment absolutely hate because it enables the sheltering of criminals, it risks the masquerade, and it's a risk to the path of humanity since practitioners need practice materials and there's no undo button, besides all the fearmongering, cultural prejudices, religious arguments and so on. <br /> <br /> <br /> Just thinking about it: Maybe the vampire could put themselves into a skinsuit and walk around during the day. And by skinsuit I mean a large person that's still alive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T12:07:12-07:00","id":1512992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1512776-can-a-vampire-build-himself-a-living-body-with-vicissitude-6?p=1512990#post1512990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just thinking about it: Maybe the vampire could put themselves into a skinsuit and walk around during the day. And by skinsuit I mean a large person that's still alive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not? And even if you can't stay awake, you could still use a retainer as a mobile haven. Put two handfuls of soil in their pockets (or make a little abscess inside the body and put it there (assuming this doesn't cause an infection)), rearrange the tissues to make space and climb in. Since vicissitude alterations defy the nightly reset, there's no reason this shouldn't extend to bloodform, and you can fit far more comfortably in a person as a liquid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T13:45:05-07:00","id":1513004,"title":"","content":"Personally I prefer the idea of rebuilding a physiology with living tissues that truly became part of the vampire. The &quot;skinsuite&quot; is a good idea but doesn't make the vampire truly more &quot;living&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8595-conradine","name":"Conradine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8595_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-27T17:54:40-07:00","id":1513018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1512776-can-a-vampire-build-himself-a-living-body-with-vicissitude-6?p=1512967#post1512967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> In the deffense of Vicissitude (and any other Discipline) it is not the power itself that is &quot;bad&quot; or &quot;unbalanced&quot;, but 99% of te time it is the players who tend to forget, Vampire is a personal horror game and the Disciplines <i>are part of the Curse , </i>steering you away from who you were, from Humanity, slowly degenerating you in to something not even remotely human and not &quot;superpowers&quot; ready to abuse</div> </div> </div> </div>My issues are as much with power creep as with just for shock body horror. And this doesn't come only from players, but also from many official book writters. Did we really need a cathedral of flesh? How does that relate to the vampire myths, or the original themes and gothic punk of the game?<br /> I actually remember liking the Discipline when it was first released in 2nd edition, it had a Dracula shapeshifter vibe and it has potential to create paranoia by taking other people's visages.<br /> And that's why I haven't completely got rid of it. I have made it into a Koldunic Path and Rituals that allows only some minor alterations to the self.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T00:50:06-07:00","id":1513050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Microcuchon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1512776-can-a-vampire-build-himself-a-living-body-with-vicissitude-6?p=1513018#post1513018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does that relate to the vampire myths, or the original themes and gothic punk of the game?.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually?<br /> In several ways<br /> <br /> In South Slavic folklore, a vampire was believed to pass through several distinct stages in its development. The first 40 days were considered decisive for the making of a vampire; it started out as an invisible shadow and then gradually gained strength from the lifeblood of the living, forming a (typically invisible) jelly-like, boneless mass, and eventually building up a human-like body nearly identical to the one the person had had in life. This development allowed the creature to ultimately leave its grave and begin a new life as a human. The vampire, who was usually male, was also sexually active and could have children, either with his widow or a new wife. These could become vampires themselves, but could also have a special ability to see and kill vampires, allowing them to become vampire hunters.<br /> The bodies of <i>vrykolakas</i> have the same distinctive characteristics as the bodies of vampires in Balkan folklore. They do not decay; instead, they swell and may even attain a &quot;drumlike&quot; form, being very large, have a ruddy complexion, and are, according to one account, &quot;fresh and gorged with new blood&quot;.\u200b in Greek folklore, the <i>vrykolakas</i> are described more as cannibals than bloodsuckers with a taste in particular for human livers\u200b<br /> <br /> This a bit obsucre slavic folklore was - I think - where the Tzimisce and their power came from<br /> And of course, the &quot;changing body&quot; is somewhat the base of every vampiric myth; - the natural characteristics of decomposition\u2014such as receding gums and the appearance of growing hair and fingernails\u2014reinforced the belief that corpses were in fact continuing some manner of life after death and transform<br /> <br /> As for the power itself, it actually fits in the following folklore and many other<br /> <br /> Whereas Protean merely enables a Cainite to emulate God's creatures, this twisted power allows a Tzimisce to defile and deform those creatures<br /> \u200bGod's curse is reflected in Vicissitude in that it replaces the ability to <i>nurture</i> and <i>care</i> with the ability to <i>rend and corrupt</i>.<br /> Vicissitude takes the power of creation, how God created Adam and Lilith... the Crone... Eve! Thats it, Eve! Adam and Eve from the living earth, formed them like a sculptor using clay, Vicissitude twist this holy creation with the twisting and shaping God's perfect creation - after all, Genesis told us, God created man in his own image<br /> <br /> But of course, this is my two cents in the matter <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T02:08:36-07:00","id":1514433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1512776-can-a-vampire-build-himself-a-living-body-with-vicissitude-6?p=1512992#post1512992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why not? And even if you can't stay awake, you could still use a retainer as a mobile haven. Put two handfuls of soil in their pockets (or make a little abscess inside the body and put it there (assuming this doesn't cause an infection)), rearrange the tissues to make space and climb in. Since vicissitude alterations defy the nightly reset, there's no reason this shouldn't extend to bloodform, and you can fit far more comfortably in a person as a liquid.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds like Conquering Blood from Player's Guide to High Clans - Dominate 5 Vicissitude 5. You enter a person in blood form and pilot them from the inside.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12911-lateral-psychotropy","name":"Lateral.Psychotropy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-11T17:01:19-07:00","id":1514640,"title":"","content":"I\u2019ve always thought Vicissitude could also be an amazing help to the Masquerade, or at least helping vampires avoid hunters. Second Inquisition learned your appearance? Cool, for the cost of a boon, he\u2019s an entirely new identity and face, complete with papers. A body-double matching your old appearance has just publicly died. Enjoy your new unlife. <br /> <br /> Honestly, a Tzimisce who was willing to join the Camarilla, and use his Vicissitude only for post-mortem \u201cplastic surgery\u201d would probably become near invaluable in his domain, although would have to jump through\u2026 just so many hoops to be there. <br /> <br /> As for a \u201cskinsuit\u201d, my interpretation is that it\u2019s theoretically possible, but just a layer of skin isn\u2019t enough. Skin is slightly translucent, just like you can see blood vessels under your skin, if the layer is thin enough to see the vampire beneath, they\u2019re going to burn. If you\u2019re going for a \u201cspace suit\u201d type thing you could get around having a thicker layer of proper flesh over your torso/limbs, but the extremities cause issues, particularly the head. Best bet is probably to turn yourself into a torso, then ride around inside a ghoul like Krang, and use Dominate to control your flesh-puppet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27967-caerolion","name":"Caerolion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-19T21:33:23-07:00","id":1515620,"title":"","content":"No. Graft Life to Life fully incorporates the new part into the recipient's body. If the recipient is alive, it's a living part incorporated into a living body; if the recipient is undead, it becomes an undead part incorporated into an undead body. Hence the comparative ease of attaching limbs to vampiric bodies: there's no pesky &quot;compatibility&quot; concerns.<br /> <br /> Either way, it's a real &quot;going around your ass to get to your elbow&quot; way to do things for a Tzimisce, if for some reason they want to knock around in a mortal body for a while. Especially an elder. It's easier and more efficient to just possess a szlachta or vozhd via Animalism, or any mortal via Dominate (it's a common discipline, popular among elder Tzimisce, and even in-clan for the old farts).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}